{"url": "https://www.ohsu.edu/school-of-medicine/biomedical-sciences-graduate-program/program-curriculum", "final_url": "https://www.ohsu.edu/school-of-medicine/biomedical-sciences-graduate-program/program-curriculum", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-29", "text": "Program Curriculum | OHSU\nSkip to main content\nSkip to main navigation\nSchool of Medicine\nGraduate Program in Biomedical Sciences\nMenu\nEnter keywords\nAbout\nContact Us\nAdmissions\nRecruitment\nProgram Curriculum\nResearch Hubs\nBiochemical, Molecular and Structural Biology (BMSB)\nChemical Biology and Cellular Physiology (CBCP)\nDevelopment, Differentiation and Disease (D3)\nGenome Sciences (GS)\nIntegrated Cancer Biology (ICB)\nInfectious Disease and Immunology (IDI)\nAcademic Mentors\nFaculty\nInterdisciplinary Training Opportunities\nResources\nOHSU Home\nFind a Doctor\nMyChart\nDonate\nJobs\nDirections\nContact\nHome\nGraduate Program in Biomedical Sciences (PBMS)\nProgram Curriculum\nGraduate Program in Biomedical Sciences (PBMS)\nGraduate Program in Biomedical Sciences (PBMS)\nAbout\nContact Us\nAdmissions\nRecruitment\nProgram Curriculum\nResearch Hubs\nBiochemical, Molecular and Structural Biology (BMSB)\nChemical Biology and Cellular Physiology (CBCP)\nDevelopment, Differentiation and Disease (D3)\nGenome Sciences (GS)\nIntegrated Cancer Biology (ICB)\nInfectious Disease and Immunology (IDI)\nAcademic Mentors\nFaculty\nInterdisciplinary Training Opportunities\nResources\nProgram Curriculum\nPBMS is meant to be a flexible program where the educational training plan is custom-built for each student based on their research project and trajectory. Course requirements reflect our desire that students receive a strong scientific foundation in core biomedical disciplines and learn to think critically about their own project and the work of others. Recognizing that graduates in the biomedical sciences follow many trajectories, we provide training in analytical, professional and communication skills that will prepare students for diverse scientific careers.\nPBMS Course Listing\nFall 2024 Schedule\nPBMS Fall Term Curriculum Overview\nBased on your academic background and with the advice of your Academic Mentors, you take 2 core courses (Genetics, and Cell Biology) and 1 of 4 electives (Chemical Biology innovators, Principles of Physiology, Molecular Biophysics and Structural Bioinformatics and Fundamentals of Immunology). Note: The other core PBMS course Biochemistry will be offered Fall 2025.\nYou may choose to take all 3 Core Courses instead of choosing 1 of the elective courses.\nRequired Courses:\nBMSC 665 Scientific Logic\nBMSC 664 Research Models and Methods\nMGRD 650 The Practice and Ethics of Science\nTake Two of Three PBMS Core Courses:\nBMSC 661 Structure & Function Of Bio Molecules (Offered Fall 2025)\nBMSC 663 Cellular Biology\nBMSC 662 Genetic Mechanisms and Bioregulation\nChoose One of Five Elective Courses:\nBMSC 666 Chemical Biology Innovators\nBMSC 667 Principles of Physiology\nBMSC 668 Molecular Biophysics and Structural Bioinformatics\nBMSC 669 Fundamentals of Immunology\nPHPH 618 Receptor Pharmacology\nOregon Health & Science University is dedicated to improving the health and quality of life for all Oregonians through excellence, innovation and leadership in health care, education and research.\n\u00a9 2001-2026 Oregon Health & Science University. OHSU is an equal opportunity affirmative action institution.\nNotice of Privacy Practices\nNotice of Nondiscrimination\nOHSU Home\nContact\nEspa\u00f1ol\nRussian | \u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439\nAbout OHSU\nMaps and Directions\nJobs\nMake a Gift\nWebsite Accessibility\nIntegrity\nDiversity and Inclusion\nOffice of Civil Rights Investigations and Compliance\nTitle IX\nVolunteer\nPatient Resources\nBilling and Insurance\nFind a Doctor\nFind a Clinic\nFor Patients and Visitors\nClinical Trials\nPrice Transparency\nNo Surprise Billing\nResearch\nAbout\nAdministratio